  "problem": "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x=2$ $\\,$ $Q(x):$ ${x}^{2}=4$\n\nConsider the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ above. Which of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x)⇒Q(x)?$\n\n- ${x}^{2}=4$ implies $x=2$\n- If ${x}^{2}=4,$ then $x=2$\n- ${x}^{2}=4$ only if $x=2$\n- ${x}^{2}=4$ if $x=2$",
